000110465926058670/0001104659-26-058670-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-058670"},{"text":"Debt of $365.8m against equity of $336.1m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1860543/000110465926058670/0001104659-26-058670-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-058670"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 3.0% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (300,000 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1860543/000110465926076823/0001104659-26-076823-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 31.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.31,"consecutive":2,"current":0.387,"current_display":"38.7%","threshold_display":"31.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 4.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.04,"consecutive":2,"current":0.195,"current_display":"19.5%","threshold_display":"4.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 13.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.13,"consecutive":1,"current":0.058